## TokenLighten MCP (compact)

Root `AGENTS.md` owns active designs/plan. Edit canonical templates and regenerate AI rules; never edit generated blocks.

Three tools: `read_file`, `edit_file`, `search_files`. Start EVERY file task with TL; unknown-location/multi-file=>`read_file {query:"<verbatim request>",task:{epoch:"new"}}` before native reads or Explore-style subagents; never truncate. If TL is unavailable or the host reports native-bypass, use native and never activate TL mid-task. Same-task narrow re-packs may be incomplete. Search: `action:"find",queries:["<one identifier>"]`; batch several in one `queries=[…]`; use known-subtree `scope.path`, else repo-wide.
<!-- tl-legacy-compat:start -->
Legacy only: `mode`/`paths`/`handles`/`maxBytes`/`maxTokens`/`taskProfile`/`taskEpoch` require TL_LEGACY_INPUT=accept; RC uses refuse. Never emit them; returned `next` is canonical.
<!-- tl-legacy-compat:end -->
Every call: own `cwd` (or `cwd-required-for-edit`); shared workspace: fixed `lane`. A known single edit may fast-close; otherwise use one `edit_file` `edits[]` batch, each item owning its target.
An unrecognized `kind`=SAFE-STOP: report it, issue no edit, never infer from its fields.
Act on `read.task_pack`'s `decision.kind`: `act.answer`/`act.edit` closes discovery; use served evidence and batch ready edits once. A `refusal`'s `retry` is the only transition. Every `next` is a whole executable call — run verbatim; hints are advisory, never execute them as calls. A `read.receipt` is never a re-pack cue: follow `next` when present, otherwise act or stop on restated evidence/certificate. Stop after a passing relevant check. Reads accept `budget.bytes`/`budget.tokens`.
Everything else — artifact/archive specifics, verification-kit detail, per-kind deep rules — arrives on-demand inside the response that needs it; complete only until one does.
<!-- tokenlighten:mcp-instructions:end -->
